# Documentation MyClub

## SoT
- Notion: product, domain, UX, durable decisions summary on reference pages.
- Git: code, HTTP contract, local persistence, active i18n conventions.
- Both: Notion = intent; Git = operational detail; cross-link required.
- One normative truth = one SoT elsewhere = link only.

## Reference pages
- Describe current truth + active constraints. No phase numbers in titles.
- Reference pages = current product truth; phase capitalization lives in Tasks / Decisions (not on reference pages).
- Extra nesting only for large autonomous topics (e.g. Cockpit, Domaine).
- Play’Up UX surfaces / chrome (PE Spec, Accueil, Shell, i18n, Cockpit) nest under hub **Expérience produit**; Identité stays top-level under Play’Up (transversal DS).
- Do not create a page if SoT already exists; enrich instead.

## When to update docs
- Code-only change, truth unchanged → Git only.
- Product/domain/UX/architecture truth changes → update Notion reference page.
- Durable trade-off → Decision DB row + `SoT → [[page]]` in body + update reference.
- Not every task requires doc updates.

## Tasks & phases
- Tasks = short action + SoT link. Optional `[Play'Up][Phase X.Y]` in title.
- Phases never structure product navigation.

## Archive
- Old phase pages: ARCHIVE banner, remove from sidebars, no archive index.
- Delete only after human review confirms SoT migrated.

## On close
- Fix Play'Up status paragraph if false; fix README if public summary false.
